# 2. Executive verdict

## 2.1 Disposition

2.1.1 verdict=`REJECT-AS-TRD2-DEFINITION-REQUIREMENT-BASELINE`.

2.1.2 `Gate29=BLOCKED`; `Development freeze=ACTIVE`; `Materialization permit=ABSENT`; `Product/Git/Provider side effects=BLOCKED`.

2.1.3 exact findings=`20`: `P0=9`, `P1=9`, `P2=2`, `P3=0`.

2.1.4 all 20 findings are independent review observations and remain `OPEN`. Similar titles, shared sources or shared remediation do not merge their identities.

2.1.5 the subject is materially stronger than TRD-1 in deterministic identities, detached acceptance, retention planning, Public-repository intent and fail-closed language. It still cannot safely become the complete Definition baseline because security-critical source closure, authority chronology, side-effect identities, review reconciliation and product-boundary semantics remain non-total.

## 2.2 Decisive causes

2.2.1 the source graph contains five explicitly referenced identities that do not exist in their named frozen source namespaces, while numerous real review identities are absent as explicit references.

2.2.2 only 11 of 24 MSSA identities appear as individually enumerable references. The remaining 13 appear only through a range at §11.2.3 even though §1.3.3 itself says ranges are navigation only.

2.2.3 the D18-A2 artifact root is not a member of §1.2 even though Public visibility is made binding by §4.5 and §9.3.

2.2.4 the exact Source-to-Legal-to-Permit-to-Capture chronology, one-to-one risky capability/side-effect instances and Message/Intent/Operation/Attempt state machine are absent.

2.2.5 the Finding/review/reconciliation contract is not total, P0/P1 risk acceptance is not prohibited, and §11.2.4 can textually permit a Candidate acceptance path while P0/P1/P2 findings are merely “explicitly blocking”.

2.2.6 tenant/auth/BFF, Meta/rate/one-attempt, AI, file, supply-chain/SSRF/deployment, recovery and no-fabrication boundaries are named in a catch-all corpus but are not defined as separate normative instance contracts.

