# 4. P0 findings

## 4.1 `TRD2-SHR-F001` — Source identity closure is invalid

4.1.1 severity=`P0`.

4.1.2 locator=`subject:§§1.2,1.3.2-1.3.3,sourceIds throughout,especially §§7.2-7.3,8.1-8.4`; evidence=`review:§3.2`.

4.1.3 defect=`five referenced report-local IDs do not exist in their named frozen namespaces; additional existing source findings are omitted; retention/backup clauses also bind source IDs whose actual source titles concern different defects`.

4.1.4 impact=`a parser can resolve a requirement to no source, the wrong source or an invented source identity while still reporting source coverage`.

4.1.5 required remediation=`define a root-qualified SourceFindingRef=(artifactRawRoot,reportLocalId,semanticRevision); enumerate only identities present in that exact root; reject dangling, range-only and semantically mismatched edges`.

4.1.6 safe terminal=`SOURCE-GRAPH-INVALID; no Candidate freeze`.

4.1.7 source basis=`TRD self-audit identity set; MPSA/MSAF/MSSA manifests; MSSA-F011, MSSA-F012, MSSA-F022`.

## 4.2 `TRD2-SHR-F002` — The 24-security-finding union is not preserved one-to-one

4.2.1 severity=`P0`.

4.2.2 locator=`subject:§§1.2.7,1.3.2-1.3.3,11.2.3`; evidence=`review:§3.2.3-3.2.4`.

4.2.3 defect=`13/24 MSSA identities have no individually enumerable source edge; a catch-all range is explicitly non-machine-authoritative under the subject's own contract`.

4.2.4 impact=`critical controls for source/legal capture, recovery, capability instances, Next, framework lock, tenant/auth, Meta/rate, AI/file, retention/recovery, supply chain, no-fabrication, operation lineage and authority separation can disappear without an orphan error`.

4.2.5 required remediation=`materialize an exact 24-row immutable crosswalk from every MSSA identity to one or more TRD2 requirements, its defect-preserving semantics and named safe terminal; preserve reviewer-local identity even when one requirement addresses several findings`.

4.2.6 safe terminal=`SECURITY-UNION-INCOMPLETE; no Definition acceptance`.

4.2.7 source basis=`MSSA-F001–MSSA-F024 as 24 distinct local observations`.

## 4.3 `TRD2-SHR-F003` — D18-A2 is asserted without freezing its exact decision artifact

4.3.1 severity=`P0`.

4.3.2 locator=`subject:§§1.2,4.5,9.3`; external locator=`D18-A2:§1.1;source-precedence:§3.2`.

4.3.3 defect=`the subject makes Public visibility binding but §1.2 omits the exact D18-A2 artifact root; the unaccepted source-precedence ledger cannot substitute for the missing decision bytes`.

4.3.4 impact=`Public can become an unrooted literal, a stale Private requirement can reappear, or Git governance can be evaluated against an authority claim not present in the Candidate source root`.

4.3.5 required remediation=`admit the exact D18-A2 raw root with A1/A2 authority, claim limit and supersession edge; keep the source-precedence ledger explicitly draft/unaccepted until a durable user-authority observation is bound`.

4.3.6 safe terminal=`D18-SOURCE-UNBOUND; Public remains intended but no Git/Gate credit is issued`.

4.3.7 source basis=`D18-A2 root 448cf2…; MSSA-F004, MSSA-F013, MSSA-F014`.

## 4.4 `TRD2-SHR-F004` — Source→Legal→Permit→Capture chronology is not defined

4.4.1 severity=`P0`.

4.4.2 locator=`subject:§§4.1,4.6-4.8,5.1,5.6,7.1,10.6`.

4.4.3 defect=`legal/capture state and provider observations are fields, but no atomic chronology binds the same bytes, legal disposition, account entitlement, capability revision and authority epoch through the network attempt`.

4.4.4 impact=`Terms, law, role, consent, asset, geography, quality or rate can change after review while a stale permit still authorizes a side effect`.

4.4.5 required remediation=`define distinct immutable stages MetadataObservation→LegalAssessment→LegalPermit→CapturePermit→AuthorizedCapture→RawDigest→SourceVerification→Parse→SourceUse→SourceSeal→CapabilityProfile→PreExecutionCASPermit→Attempt→ProviderFact/Capture, including exact roots, effectiveAt, expiresAt and authorityEpoch`.

4.4.6 safe terminal=`SOURCE-USE-BLOCKED; capability remains disabled`.

4.4.7 source basis=`MSSA-F005, MSSA-F012, MSSA-F023`.

## 4.5 `TRD2-SHR-F005` — Capability, side-effect and attempt identities are not one-to-one

4.5.1 severity=`P0`.

4.5.2 locator=`subject:§§3.6,4.9,5.2,6.1,6.8,11.2`.

4.5.3 defect=`the manifest names capability packages and routes but does not require one exact instance record for each external or irreversible mutation, nor one formal Message→Intent→Operation→Attempt lineage`.

4.5.4 impact=`a permit for WhatsApp send can bleed into template/media/billing/email/delete/connector operations; an ambiguous result can be blindly retried or relabeled as a new business intent`.

4.5.5 required remediation=`define CapabilityInstance and SideEffectInstance with operation, asset, credential, transport, scope, permit, authority epoch, unknown-outcome ledger, kill, reachability and five-mode tests; define exactly one provider attempt per independently approved intent unless the earlier attempt is provably not-started`.

4.5.6 safe terminal=`CAPABILITY-INSTANCE-UNBOUND; route unimported/disabled; UNKNOWN outcome receives no retry`.

4.5.7 source basis=`MSSA-F007, MSSA-F016, MSSA-F021`.

## 4.6 `TRD2-SHR-F006` — Review and reconciliation schema is not total

4.6.1 severity=`P0`.

4.6.2 locator=`subject:§§1.2.5-1.2.7,6.4,10.1-10.3,12.1.2`.

4.6.3 defect=`§6.4 lacks a root-qualified reviewer-local identity and an explicit failureBoundary; §§10.1-10.3 do not enumerate a complete review envelope or a versioned total normalization schema; §12.1.2 relies on an unnamed, unrooted intake state`.

4.6.4 impact=`two short manifests with incompatible fields can be called normalized, distinct observations can collide, a failed assertion can be placed in the wrong boundary, and a reconciler can appear to have compared records that were never eligible for comparison`.

4.6.5 required remediation=`freeze the exact reconciliation protocol root; define complete ReviewEnvelope and Finding schemas including raw review/subject roots, reviewDomain, local identity, affected identity sets, cause, exploit/failure path, failureBoundary, safe terminal, assertion coverage, claim limits and reviewer disposition; require two independently implemented normalizers over the same schema version`.

4.6.6 safe terminal=`RECONCILIATION-INELIGIBLE; strict local union preserved without equivalence or closure`.

4.6.7 source basis=`MSSA-F002, MSSA-F003, MSSA-F009, MSSA-F024; subject's own §12.1.2`.

## 4.7 `TRD2-SHR-F007` — P0/P1 risk acceptance remains possible

4.7.1 severity=`P0`.

4.7.2 locator=`subject:§§6.4,10.4,11.2.4`.

4.7.3 defect=`§10.4.4 forbids only silent P0 acceptance. It does not prohibit explicit RiskAcceptance for P0 or P1, and does not require evidence-based reclassification plus retest before a lower effective severity is considered`.

4.7.4 impact=`a blocking security defect can be administratively accepted or downgraded without reducing exposure, applying a fix or proving the change`.

4.7.5 required remediation=`make RiskAcceptance structurally impossible while effective severity is P0/P1; permit only a detached, expiring P2/P3 record after fact-based reclassification, two independent reviewers, threat evidence and retest; preserve original severity forever`.

4.7.6 safe terminal=`RISK-ACCEPTANCE-FORBIDDEN; veto stays open`.

4.7.7 source basis=`MSSA-F009, MSSA-F022`.

## 4.8 `TRD2-SHR-F008` — Definition acceptance predicate admits blocking findings

4.8.1 severity=`P0`.

4.8.2 locator=`subject:§11.2.4`, with authority interaction at `§§6.3,10.4-10.5`.

4.8.3 defect=`the terminal predicate says all P0/P1/P2 findings may be “closed or explicitly blocking” while detached approval and protected Acceptance succeed`.

4.8.4 impact=`a parser can truthfully mark a P0 as blocking and still satisfy the sentence that governs acceptance, defeating VetoSet and Gate29 separation`.

4.8.5 required remediation=`separate conformance reporting from Candidate acceptance: an open effective P0/P1, unresolved P0/P1/P2 review disagreement, ineligible review envelope or open veto must make DefinitionAcceptance impossible; blocked observations may be reported but never satisfy the acceptance conjunction`.

4.8.6 safe terminal=`CANDIDATE-REJECTED; no Acceptance envelope and no materialization permit`.

4.8.7 source basis=`MSSA-F001, MSSA-F002, MSSA-F009; BCA2-REQ-041–044`.

## 4.9 `TRD2-SHR-F009` — Five-mode assurance is not required per risky instance

4.9.1 severity=`P0`.

4.9.2 locator=`subject:§§5.4-5.5,6.8,10.6,11.2`.

4.9.3 defect=`negative and mutation tests are first-class, while Positive, Failure, Concurrency and Recovery are not five distinct required Test identities mapped to every risky capability, side-effect, Control and Threat`.

4.9.4 impact=`a capability can appear covered by a generic attack corpus while its timeout, race, ambiguous outcome, disable/recovery or rollback path was never exercised`.

4.9.5 required remediation=`add a finite TestMode enum and require separate positiveTestIds, negativeTestIds, failureTestIds, concurrencyTestIds and recoveryTestIds on every risky CapabilityInstance, SideEffectInstance, Control, Threat and adapter; each binds expected safe terminal, observed root and independent review`.

4.9.6 safe terminal=`TEST-COVERAGE-INCOMPLETE; risky instance remains disabled`.

4.9.7 source basis=`MSSA-F006, MSSA-F007`.

# 5. P1 findings

## 5.1 `TRD2-SHR-F010` — Tenant/Auth/BFF boundary is only a corpus label

5.1.1 severity=`P1`.

5.1.2 locator=`subject:§§5.6,6.6,9.1,11.2.1`.

5.1.3 defect=`no normative contract requires server-derived tenant identity, route/trust/session matrix, Clerk organization/MFA export, membership freshness, RLS matrix, CSRF/session controls, Preview→Prod isolation or denial of direct Railway ingress`.

5.1.4 impact=`BOLA, stale membership, cross-tenant access, session riding, RLS bypass and direct backend reachability remain representable as apparently complete work`.

5.1.5 required remediation=`define TenantBoundary, IdentityEnvelope, SessionBoundary, RouteTrust and IngressPolicy records with live evidence, owners, X24 dependencies, deny-by-default transitions and five-mode coverage`.

5.1.6 safe terminal=`PRIVILEGED-ROUTE-DISABLED`.

5.1.7 source basis=`MSSA-F015`.

## 5.2 `TRD2-SHR-F011` — Meta/WhatsApp rate and one-attempt policy is non-normative

5.2.1 severity=`P1`.

5.2.2 locator=`subject:§§4.7,6.6-6.8,7.1,11.2.1`; refresh=`Cyber/Public refresh §4`.

5.2.3 defect=`the exact Test WABA/phone/template/recipient asset graph, live quality and rate snapshots, layered minimum calculation, cap-zero fallback, provider/webhook fact reconciliation and blind-retry prohibition are absent`.

5.2.4 impact=`wrong asset or credential, stale consent/rate/quality, duplicate attempt, false sent status or retry after unknown provider outcome can reach the design`.

5.2.5 required remediation=`define MetaAssetGraph, RatePolicySnapshot, LayeredRateDecision and OneAttemptLedger bound to exact account/number/release roots; require Tal-owned policy source and keep outbound cap zero when live evidence is stale, 429, conflicting or unavailable`.

5.2.6 safe terminal=`WHATSAPP-OUTBOUND-CAP=0; no provider attempt`.

5.2.7 source basis=`MSSA-F016, MSSA-F021; Cyber refresh §§4.1.2-4.1.6`.

## 5.3 `TRD2-SHR-F012` — AI safety/off-state is not a Definition contract

5.3.1 severity=`P1`.

5.3.2 locator=`subject:§§4.5,4.10,11.2.1`; Cyber refresh=`§2.2.4-2.2.6`.

5.3.3 defect=`Human-approval-only AI is mentioned as a Decision example, but no schema requires AI-off, hosted-tools-off, autonomous-side-effects-off, draft-only output, provider privacy/data-use evidence, prompt/data classification, tenant isolation, eval provenance or kill semantics`.

5.3.4 impact=`provider use, false ZDR/privacy claims, prompt injection, cross-tenant retrieval or autonomous action can be omitted from completeness while AI remains named in scope`.

5.3.5 required remediation=`define AICapabilityProfile and AIProviderEvidence with explicit disabled defaults, human approval boundary, allowed data classes, tool/action reachability, eval/AISVS mapping, revocation and five-mode tests`.

5.3.6 safe terminal=`AI-DISABLED; no autonomous side effect`.

5.3.7 source basis=`MSSA-F017; current D02/D25 planning posture; Cyber refresh §2.2`.

## 5.4 `TRD2-SHR-F013` — File and knowledge pipeline safety is absent

5.4.1 severity=`P1`.

5.4.2 locator=`subject:§§6.6,8.1,11.2.1`.

5.4.3 defect=`no normative object lifecycle covers upload-off, quarantine, immutable object version/checksum, scanner result, TBAC, parser sandbox/no-network policy, derived chunk/vector lineage, tenant isolation, cascade deletion and recovery`.

5.4.4 impact=`malicious content can be released, parsers can escape, derived data can survive source deletion, or cross-tenant knowledge can be retrieved`.

5.4.5 required remediation=`define FileObject, ScanVerdict, ParserExecution, DerivedKnowledge and CascadeDisposition records; bind every transition to exact object version and keep Upload/Knowledge disabled until provider/scanner/storage decisions are admitted`.

5.4.6 safe terminal=`UPLOAD-OFF; OBJECT-QUARANTINED; KNOWLEDGE-DISABLED`.

5.4.7 source basis=`MSSA-F017`.

## 5.5 `TRD2-SHR-F014` — Supply-chain, SSRF and Deployment boundaries lack executable semantics

5.5.1 severity=`P1`.

5.5.2 locator=`subject:§§9.3-9.4,11.2.1`; omitted specific source=`MSSA-F010,MSSA-F019`.

5.5.3 defect=`the catch-all does not require a resolved dependency graph, SBOM, provenance, verified signature/trust anchor, current Next blocker disposition, fixed-destination adapters, DNS/IP/redirect/private/link-local/metadata denial, composite Release manifest, ingress/TLS proof, canary or fixed rollback artifact`.

5.5.4 impact=`dependency/workflow compromise, vulnerable Next artifact, wrong artifact, SSRF, Preview→Prod crossing, callback takeover or vulnerable rollback remain outside deterministic closure`.

5.5.5 required remediation=`define SupplyChainSnapshot, NetworkDestinationPolicy and ReleaseArtifactSet as exact-root records; generic URL/connectors remain absent; every release and rollback binds the same verified dependency/provenance/security roots`.

5.5.6 safe terminal=`MERGE/BUILD/RELEASE/DEPLOY-BLOCKED`.

5.5.7 source basis=`MSSA-F010, MSSA-F019`.

## 5.6 `TRD2-SHR-F015` — Deletion safety omits provider saga and recovery semantics

5.6.1 severity=`P1`.

5.6.2 locator=`subject:§§8.1-8.4`.

5.6.3 defect=`the local atomic bounded plan is strong, but no contract covers multi-provider deletion saga state, irreversible partial success, provider idempotency scope, ambiguous timeout, Legal-Hold race after remote preflight, adapter disablement, reconciliation or recovery tests`.

5.6.4 impact=`a partial provider deletion or unknown outcome can be retried broadly, misreported as complete, violate Legal Hold or leave undeleted replicas`.

5.6.5 required remediation=`define one DeletionAdapterInstance and provider operation ledger per store, with pre-execution CAS, one-attempt semantics, partial/unknown state, compensating disposition, reconciliation and five-mode tests; never infer safety from post-delete audit`.

5.6.6 safe terminal=`DELETE-ADAPTER-DISABLED; unresolved identities remain UNKNOWN and visible`.

5.6.7 source basis=`MSSA-F018; MSSA-F005–MSSA-F007`.

## 5.7 `TRD2-SHR-F016` — Backup/Restore misses ransomware and privacy-replay controls

5.7.1 severity=`P1`.

5.7.2 locator=`subject:§§8.5-8.6`.

5.7.3 defect=`exact backup/restore binding is defined, but WORM/immutability, account/credential separation, destructive-primary scenario, real retention cohort, quarantine, opt-out/deletion/unknown-operation resurrection detection, re-deletion ledger and restore privacy replay are absent`.

5.7.4 impact=`a valid digest can still represent a backup deletable by the same compromised authority or a restore that resurrects prohibited data and pending side effects`.

5.7.5 required remediation=`extend Backup Evidence with administrative separation and immutability proof; extend Restore Evidence with quarantine, policy replay, resurrection diff, re-deletion/tombstone ledger, pending-operation neutralization and real cohort observation`.

5.7.6 safe terminal=`RESTORE-NOT-USABLE; resilience/RPO/RTO/retention claim blocked`.

5.7.7 source basis=`MSSA-F018`.

## 5.8 `TRD2-SHR-F017` — X24 is use-specific in name but incomplete in lifecycle

5.8.1 severity=`P1`.

5.8.2 locator=`subject:§9.1`.

5.8.3 defect=`constructor, entropy source, length, storage, rotation and threat are present, but there is no finite use inventory or mandatory primitive, encoding, TTL, single-use, binding context, revocation, owner, tests and expiry for OAuth state, CSRF, PKCE, invitations/recovery, HMAC challenges and ephemeral keys`.

5.8.4 impact=`an exact approval can still authorize a security value whose replay, contextual binding or revocation semantics are undefined`.

5.8.5 required remediation=`define one X24UseDecision per security purpose and forbid inherited/general approval; every CSPRNG callsite resolves to exactly one approved current use; deterministic IDs remain separate; Math.random remains forbidden everywhere`.

5.8.6 safe terminal=`SECURITY-VALUE-USE-BLOCKED`.

5.8.7 source basis=`MSSA-F008`.

## 5.9 `TRD2-SHR-F018` — No-fabrication has no TestInput provenance workflow

5.9.1 severity=`P1`.

5.9.2 locator=`subject:§§5.4-5.6,8.1,9.2,10.6`; absent explicit source=`MSSA-F020`.

5.9.3 defect=`Evidence provenance is defined, but the inputs used to generate test/results lack a separate registry for source class, exact digest, data class, approval, purpose, tenant/scope, expiry, destruction receipt and downstream invalidation`.

5.9.4 impact=`real data can exceed purpose/tenant/expiry, sandbox results can masquerade as live, and invented business data can enter a derived Evidence chain`.

5.9.5 required remediation=`define TestInputProvenance and DerivedResultLineage; normative public standard vectors are distinct from business data; missing provenance rejects the result; no fake/mock/demo/sample/synthetic business data receives readiness Evidence credit`.

5.9.6 safe terminal=`EVIDENCE-REJECTED; dependent results invalidated`.

5.9.7 source basis=`MSSA-F020`.

# 6. P2 findings

## 6.1 `TRD2-SHR-F019` — Public Git profile is underspecified despite correct Public intent

6.1.1 severity=`P2`, promoted to `P0` if a Push/Merge/Release/Deploy edge becomes reachable before hardening.

6.1.2 locator=`subject:§§3.8,9.2-9.4`; D18=`§§2-5`; Cyber refresh=`§3`.

6.1.3 defect=`§9.3 summarizes governance but does not enumerate the required Public profile and negative matrix: deny direct/force/delete/bypass, stale approvals, CODEOWNERS enforcement, Actions allowlist/full-SHA/least privilege/fork-secret safety, OIDC, secret/history/LFS scans, push protection bypass, CodeQL, Dependabot disposition, SECURITY.md, private vulnerability reporting, License/NOTICE and wrong-root rejection`.

6.1.4 impact=`a future implementation can satisfy a broad “policy present” field while the currently observed main-unprotected/rulesets-zero/scanning-disabled condition remains`.

6.1.5 required remediation=`materialize a versioned PublicRepoHardeningProfile with every control, current live observation, compensating-control policy and positive/negative/failure/concurrency/recovery readback; Public visibility itself remains intended and must not be changed as remediation`.

6.1.6 safe terminal=`NO PUSH; NO MERGE; NO RELEASE; repository remains Public`.

6.1.7 source basis=`MSSA-F004, MSSA-F013, MSSA-F014; D18-A2; Cyber refresh §3`.

## 6.2 `TRD2-SHR-F020` — Dynamic-source roles and official-source capture are incomplete

6.2.1 severity=`P2`.

6.2.2 locator=`subject:§§2.1,4.1,4.6-4.7,5.1,5.6,10.6,10.7`.

6.2.3 defect=`Source authority class does not explicitly separate retrievedBy, sourceVerifiedBy, legalDispositionBy, accountCapabilityVerifiedBy and approvedForUseBy; framework URLs/versions and mutable provider observations are not required to carry captured official bytes or an explicit unavailable root before use`.

6.2.4 impact=`retrieval accuracy can be mistaken for legal applicability, account entitlement or approval, and a “latest” URL can change while an old claim stays current`.

6.2.5 required remediation=`define separate authority appointments for the five roles; bind exact captured content/API response roots, checkedAt, expiry, change trigger, claim limits and unavailable terminal; never promote a dated document observation to live account proof`.

6.2.6 safe terminal=`SOURCE-USE-BLOCKED; live entitlement remains UNKNOWN`.

6.2.7 source basis=`MSSA-F011, MSSA-F012, MSSA-F023`.

# 7. Controls that materially improved over TRD-1

## 7.1 Positive observations with strict claim limits

7.1.1 §§2.2–2.6 explicitly separate same-generation authority, work domains, detached acceptance and materialization permits. This is a sound direction, but it does not close Findings 006–008.

7.1.2 §§3.1–3.9 define total scalar intent, canonical bytes, domain-separated roots, deterministic IDs, immutable versions and workspace path protection. The internal TRD2 requirement graph is acyclic in this snapshot.

7.1.3 §§8.1–8.4 correctly require DataClass lifecycle separation, trigger legality, active/Hold exclusions, short-lived rooted deletion plans, mutation-time checks and post-delete verification as audit only.

7.1.4 §§8.5–8.6 correctly bind Restore to an exact backup and object digests rather than treating a command-success receipt as proof.

7.1.5 §9.1 correctly separates deterministic content IDs from security-purpose randomness and explicitly forbids `Math.random()`.

7.1.6 §§9.2–9.4 correctly preserve Public visibility, reject the outer Git root and deny a general Push permit.

7.1.7 §12 retains the safe disposition: zero requirement credit, Gate29 blocked and development freeze active. This prevents the present draft from self-authorizing Product work.

# 8. Official-source refresh requirements

## 8.1 Dated refresh required before any future claim

8.1.1 Meta official documentation and exact live WABA/phone/template/quality/rate/Graph-version observations require a new authorized capture. The 2026-08-29 refresh returned HTTP 429 for 4/4 attempted pages and grants no freshness extension.

8.1.2 GitHub repository settings require fresh signed/readable API exports bound to canonical repo root, remote and head before any governance claim; current observed deficits remain planning inputs only.

8.1.3 NIST CSF, SSDF, incident response and digital-identity versions; OWASP ASVS/API/AISVS/Agentic catalogues; CIS Controls; and GitHub feature documentation require captured exact version/content roots and role-limited crosswalks before Gate use. A `latest` URL is discovery only.

8.1.4 Next.js/security advisory and full resolved dependency graph require a dated official/vendor source refresh before selecting any corrected version. This review does not assert a replacement version.

8.1.5 Clerk, Vercel, Railway, OpenAI, object-storage, malware-scanning, queue, database, backup and monitoring documentation/account state require exact official-source plus live-account observations only if their capability is admitted. Documentation alone does not prove entitlement.

8.1.6 Meta Terms, data protection, retention, Legal Hold, jurisdiction and provider processing claims require named Legal authority. Researcher or source verifier observation is not legal approval.

